# Keep the build context small and never ship secrets or host-built artifacts.
#
# THIS FILE MUST STAY AT THE REPO ROOT, even though the compose files now live in
# apps/backend and apps/storefront. Docker reads .dockerignore from the BUILD
# CONTEXT root, and both Dockerfiles use the repo root as their context (npm
# workspace: the lockfile and hoisted node_modules are here). Move it into an app
# folder and it is silently ignored — node_modules gets copied into every build,
# which makes them enormous and slow.
**/node_modules
**/.medusa
**/dist
**/.next
**/out
**/.turbo
**/.expo

# Secrets — the container gets its config from compose environment variables.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.template
!**/.env.example

# The mobile app is in neither image — you cannot run a phone app in a container.
# It is distributed via Expo/EAS instead.
apps/mobile

.git
.gitignore
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store

# Compose config is read by the Docker CLI on the host, never by a build.
**/docker-compose.yml
